'''Nusaraya''' ([[w:Javanese language|Mataraman]]: ꦤꦸꦱꦫꦪ) or in official form '''State of Nusaraya''' (Mataraman: ꦤꦺꦒꦫ​ꦏꦺꦱꦠꦸꦮꦤ꧀​ꦤꦸꦱꦫꦪ, '''Negara Kesatuan Nusaraya''') a sovereign state in [[North Fosia]]. With a total area of approximately 866,537 km² (334,571 sq mi). It is bordered to the south by [[Jogos]] and (BURMESE), to the east by [[Margarana]], [[Pasundan]] and [[Malayu]], to the north and west by [[Kendriyan Ocean]]. Nusaraya is the world's ??th-largest country. It is the ??th-most-populous country in the world, with around 252 million people. The capital city is [[Banjarnegara]] and largest city is [[Kertajati]].

Nusaraya is a constitutional monarchy with parliamentary system. Nusaraya monarch has its origins from 13th century First Kingdom of Nusaraya which is descendant from the late [[Kingdom of Singaraja]]. In 16th century Kingdom of Nusaraya expanded its territory to [[Nusagede Region]] annexing the major Kingdom of Lasem. After brief period of civil war and chaos, [[Hartono Dynasty]] ruled over Nusaraya and start the era of [[Empire of Nusaraya]] in 19th century. After the end of Great Adonia War, Nusarayan empire dissolved and the original territory from 19th century become the modern day State of Nusaraya in 1948.

The Nusarayan economy is the world's ?? largest GDP and ?? largest in percapita. Nusarayan economy experienced rapid growth after [[Nusaraya War]] driven by its natural resources however its currently dominated by the sectors of commerce, high tech industry and services including tourism. Nusaraya is a great power and a major regional power within North Fosia, and has been characterized as a potential superpower.
== Etymology ==
The name Nusaraya comes from the [[w:Javanese language|Mataraman]] words of Nusa (ꦤꦸꦱ) which means islands or archipelago and Raya (ꦫꦪ) means greater. Nusaraya literally translated into Greater Archipelago which consist of the realm for [[wikipedia:Javanese people|Mataraman]] from the island of [[Mataram Island|Mataram]] and its surrounding including parts of mainland [[Fosia]] which settled by Mataraman people.

The name Nusaraya first adopted by the [[First Kingdom of Nusaraya]] which founded in 1295. According to the [[w:Kakawin|Kakawin]] Kertajaya written in Palm-leaf manuscript in the crumble of [[Kingdom of Singaraja]], [[Prince Wijaya]] from late Singaraja last king [[Kertabumi III]] founded the kingdom which he envisioned to rule the realm of Mataraman islands area.
== History ==
=== Prehistory ===
=== Middle Ages ===
==== Kingdom of Kamulan ====
Kingdom of Kamulan which according to the Watugiri transcription near [[Wonogiri]] believed as the earliest known state to be associated with the Mataraman people. Founded around 470 AD, Kamulan kingdom territory emerged to rule the western part of Mataram Island and part of the [[Nusagede Region]] (mainland Fosia which inhabited by Mataraman people). Kamulan kingdom fall around 989 AD which resulting the emerge of smaller states in its former territory.
==== Warring State Period ====
==== Kingdom of Singaraja ====
[[Kingdom of Singaraja]] is one of the duchies emerged after the fall of Kamulan Kingdom in 10th century. By 1074, Singaraja kingdom under the rule of [[Wirahman II]] conquered the western part of Mataram island, known as the first state to dominate the former Kamulan Kingdom territory.
==== First Kingdom of Nusaraya ====
[[First Kingdom of Nusaraya]] accodring to Kakawin Kertajaya, founded in 1295 by [[Prince Wijaya]] from the crumble of Singaraja after the [[Daras-Singaraja War|invasion of Daras into the Pasundan Peninsula]]. First Kingdom of Nusaraya consist of the northern part of Mataraman Island with the capital in the modern day [[Slawi]]. At that point, the situation of Mataraman island similar to the pre-Singaraja kingdom situation where minor states and duchies lead by local lords. Prince Wijaya which become King Raharjo I create tributary of these minor states and try to integrate slowly into Nusaraya however the effort not really make a major movement until King Adiwijaya II rule in 15th century.

First Kingdom of Nusaraya managed to unify the fragment of former Singaraja territory on Mataraman island in 1447 under one state by [[King Adiwijaya II]] and later vassalize [[Kingdom of Atambua]] and [[Kingdom of Pajajaran]] peacefully without any major war. Adiwijaya II also managed to establish the tributary states alongside the northern coast of western [[Balausia Peninsula]].
